	    <const name="_GREATER"/>
	    <const name="_ASTERISK"/>
	</param>
    <abstract> It returns 1 if any key is pressed </abstract>
    <description>
	<p>
	    This function checks the state of a key by his position
	    code in the keyboard or scan-code, and it returns 1
	    if the key is pressed and 0 if it is not pressed.
	    The parameter can be any of the predefined constants
	    listed before.
	</p>
	<p>
	    It is important that the key codes indicate his position
	    over the keyboard, and they do not indicate to the characters
	    that hold. For example, the key _L_BRACHET corresponds to key that
	    holds the signs [, ^ and ` in the spanish keyboard, but in 
	    an english keyboard or in other language, the symbols will be
	    different. However, _L_BRACHET always corresponds to key placed at right
		of P.
	</p>
	<p>
	    If you want to guess that key has been pressed really
	    (including the symbol, that can be other if you use
	    keys like Shift or AltGr), it is necessary to consult
	    the variable <a href="ASCII"/>.
	</p>
    </description>
